note SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
note gpu/nvidia/checks/bwhz.om: the instruction decode of the scoreboard hazard checker, hz_dec of
note gpu/nvidia/om/codegen/bw_hazard.om and bw_hazard_dec.om, against the C it succeeds, omega_bw_decode of
note src/omega_bw_hazard.c at 60b5d81e (DRA-606: a scoreboard barrier field holding 6 is refused, either field).
note Composed after bw_hazard.om, bw_hazard_dec.om and gpu/nvidia/checks/lib.om; run with gpu/nvidia/checks/bwhz.tsv.
note Row, lowercase hex: d WORDS RC WBAR RBAR WAIT. hz_dec of the 16 bytes WORDS refuses (-1) exactly when RC is 1,
note and otherwise gives the write barrier, read barrier and wait mask of the C decode (record words 4, 5, 6).
note The whole check, hz_chk, takes a 3203584-word wire: more than a program may hold in local arrays, and a global
note is never an argument, so it is not run here; README.md (bwhz) says how it was compared with the C.
text t_name "BWHZ"
fn cname to void
for i ulong len t_name bound 64
ckoc ulong get t_name i
end
end
fn bzx i ulong to ulong
n = cklen i
if or eq n 0 gt n 16
ckbad
end
v = ulong 0
for j ulong n bound 16
v = or shl v 4 cknib ckch i j
end
ret v
end
fn crow to bool
if or or ne ckcnt 6 ne cklen 0 1 ne ckch 0 0 100
ckbad
end
if ne ckhexn 1 16
ckbad
end
b = new uchar 16 0
d = new ulong 24 0
for j ulong 16
put b j uchar ckhex 1 j
end
rc = hz_dec b d
rr = bzx 2
if gt rr 1
ckbad
end
if eq rr 1
ret eq rc long -1
end
if ne rc 0
ret false
end
ok = eq get d 4 bzx 3
ok = and ok eq get d 5 bzx 4
ret and ok eq get d 6 bzx 5
end
